who received the sending - I suspect some Tribes would be less disgruntled than others.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T07:19:11-07:00","id":1561416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560872-do-the-get-love-or-hate-the-norse-gods?p=1561384#post1561384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which still leaves the interesting question of how proud Garou might receive the knowledge that it was one of their Kinfolk who received the sending - I suspect some Tribes would be less disgruntled than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>About as well as the mystics trained to wield the Beast Spear took Ushio just stumbling upon it in the first episode of Ushio and Tora. Possibly, a great deal less, since most of them eventually accepted him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T14:31:09-07:00","id":1561437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560872-do-the-get-love-or-hate-the-norse-gods?p=1561416#post1561416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About as well as the mystics trained to wield the Beast Spear took Ushio just stumbling upon it in the first episode of Ushio and Tora. Possibly, a great deal less, since most of them eventually accepted him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sgt. Rage displayed proper respect towards a Metis, who died taking a silver bullet that was meant for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T22:12:48-07:00","id":1561447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560872-do-the-get-love-or-hate-the-norse-gods?p=1561437#post1561437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sgt. Rage displayed proper respect towards a Metis, who died taking a silver bullet that was meant for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this was meant for an entirely different conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T01:23:42-07:00","id":1561449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560872-do-the-get-love-or-hate-the-norse-gods?p=1561447#post1561447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like this was meant for an entirely different conversation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to point out that considering how much shit the Metis have to put up in order to earn any kind of recognition, the fact that a Get of Fenris honored his sacrifice is a good sign for Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T15:07:30-07:00","id":1561487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560872-do-the-get-love-or-hate-the-norse-gods?p=1561449#post1561449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was trying to point out that considering how much shit the Metis have to put up in order to earn any kind of recognition, the fact that a Get of Fenris honored his sacrifice is a good sign for Kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div>But Garou are still Garou with Renown and Rank, even if you think poorly of them because of their parentage. Kin don't have Renown or Rank, and will never be recognized by the spirits the way Garou are... so if something does select them, that's a pretty big upset.<br /> <br /> In further contrast, Crinos-born are basically expected to make heroic sacrifices for the greater good or to specifically save other heroes. If one dies doing this, they're considered to have gone the full distance for what Garou society sees as their purpose, however messed up that might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T15:36:00-07:00","id":1561490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560872-do-the-get-love-or-hate-the-norse-gods?p=1561487#post1561487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But Garou are still Garou with Renown and Rank, even if you think poorly of them because of their parentage. Kin don't have Renown or Rank, and will never be recognized by the spirits the way Garou are... so if something does select them, that's a pretty big upset.<br /> <br /> In further contrast, Crinos-born are basically expected to make heroic sacrifices for the greater good or to specifically save other heroes. If one dies doing this, they're considered to have gone the full distance for what Garou society sees as their purpose, however messed up that might be.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but the Metis' very existence is a direct violation of the Litany. Creating one is supposed to be forbidden by Garou law.<br /> <br /> Where as in the case of Kinfolk, it's much less severe. <i>&quot;Oooh, sorry you didn't get an active changing seed. But maybe you can ask the Dreamspeakers to teach you a bit of sorcery!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T18:05:39-07:00","id":1561495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1560872-do-the-get-love-or-hate-the-norse-gods?p=1561490#post1561490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, but the Metis' very existence is a direct violation of the Litany. Creating one is supposed to be forbidden by Garou law.<br /> <br /> Where as in the case of Kinfolk, it's much less severe. <i>&quot;Oooh, sorry you didn't get an active changing seed. But maybe you can ask the Dreamspeakers to teach you a bit of sorcery!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>First, prejudice is not a scale of more or less. It is qualitative. However lowly they see a Metis, they still see them as Garou. A spirit contacting them wouldn't be strange, and a Metis doing what is expected from a &quot;good Metis&quot; is exactly what would got praised.<br /> <br /> A Kinfolk is a Kinfolk, and one being chosen by the spirits instead of a Werewolf is a sign the spirits don't care about Garou specialness as much as they thought. No matter if the Kinfolk in question is loved by everyone, the meaning of this in their worldview is distinct and more serious.<br /> <br /> Second, they don't have this kind of relationship with the Dreamspeakers. A Kinfolk learns what kinfolk society teaches, including some Rituals within Werewolf rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}